Subject: [PATCH 11/15] =?UTF-8?q?local:=20redraw=20the=20site=20icon=20aro?=
 =?UTF-8?q?und=20the=20=E7=89=9B=E9=A9=AC=20idea?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The first attempt was four geometric strokes meant to spell 牛, but the proportions made it
read as 主 - it looked like a character, not like an ox, and said nothing about the site.

The new mark spells out 牛马 in a heavy CJK face with a sweat drop (the toil) above a shirt
collar and necktie (the office), which is the joke the site is named after. The glyphs are
baked into the images: favicon.svg embeds a PNG, so devices without CJK fonts cannot end up
showing empty boxes, and the PWA/apple icons are plain PNGs at the usual sizes.
